  [0m[1mcollisions[0m are inevitable. Hash maps resolve collisions using
  two primary techniques:

  • [0m[1mSeparate Chaining:[0m Each array bucket stores a secondary
  data structure (like a linked list or balanced search tree)
  holding all entries that share that index.
  • [0m[1mOpen Addressing:[0m If the target bucket is occupied, the map
  searches alternative slots according to a sequence (such as
  linear probing) until an empty spot is found.

  To maintain 𝒪(1) efficiency, the map monitors its [0m[1mload factor[0m
  (stored items relative to bucket count). When this exceeds a
  set threshold, the underlying array resizes—typically
  doubling in size—and all keys are rehashed.

